        "gen_ai.tool.call.arguments": "{\"content\":\"# Claim: Distributivity of doubling over addition\\n\\n## Function\\n\\nDefine a small arithmetic function `double` over the integers:\\n\\n    double(n) = n + n\\n\\n## Informal Claim\\n\\nDoubling distributes over integer addition. That is, for **all** integers `a` and `b`:\\n\\n    double(a) + double(b) = double(a + b)\\n\\nIn words: doubling two numbers separately and then adding the results gives the\\nsame value as adding the numbers first and then doubling the sum.\\n\\n## Reasoning sketch\\n\\nEach side simplifies to `2a + 2b` by the commutativity and associativity of\\ninteger addition, so the two sides must agree for every choice of `a` and `b`.\\n\\n## Formalization intent\\n\\nThis claim is intended to be verified formally, e.g., as a proof assistant\\nlemma (Lean/Coq/Isabelle) or an SMT-checked assertion, stating:\\n\\n    ∀ a b : ℤ, double a + double b = double (a + b)\\n\",\"path\":\"claim.md\"}",
